// ================================================================
// CANON-ACTOR-CODEGEN.RIO
// Practical Knowledge for Actor-Based Code Generation
// Extracted from go-run-rio.act and go-struct-rio.act
// ================================================================

Canon {
  name = actor_codegen_structure
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = architecture
  overview = "Actor-based code generators split into separate files: one for data structures, one for runtime operations, enabling clean separation of concerns."
  doc = ~~~
**Two-File Pattern:**

**File 1: Structure Definition (go-struct-rio.act)**
- Type declarations for all components
- Field definitions (data and reference pointers)
- Loader functions (parsing input into structures)
- Index building for Find/FindIn components
- GetVar() methods (introspection)
- DoIts() methods (execution dispatch)

**File 2: Runtime Operations (go-run-rio.act)**
- Reference resolution (refs() function)
- Multi-pass reference linking
- Global operation dispatcher (DoAll())
- Top-level orchestration

**Why This Split:**
- Structures can be generated/regenerated independently
- Runtime operations remain stable across schema changes
- Clear boundary between "what exists" and "how it behaves"
- Easier to maintain and debug

**Generated Structure Pattern:**
```
package main

// Global arrays holding all instances
type ActT struct {
    index map[string]int
    ApComp [] *KpComp
    ApElement [] *KpElement
    // ... one array per component type
}

// Individual component structs
type KpComp struct {
    Me int              // My index in array
    MyName string       // Key value (for Find/FindIn)
    Parent string       // Parent's key
    LineNo string       // Source location
    Comp string         // Type name
    Flags []string      // Modifiers
    Names map[string]any // All field values
    Kparentp int        // Parent pointer
    // Reference fields as pointers (K{name}p)
    // Child arrays (Its{Type})
}
```

**Key Insight:** Structure mirrors schema exactly, runtime handles traversal and resolution.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_reference_resolution_multipass
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = reference_handling
  overview = "Reference resolution requires multiple passes because derived references depend on previously resolved references."
  doc = ~~~
**The Multi-Pass Algorithm:**

**Pass 1 - Direct References:**
```go
// ref: Global lookup in Find index
err, res = fnd3(act, "Component_" + value, value, "ref:...", check, lineNo, lno)
st.K{name}p = res

// link: Parent-scoped lookup in FindIn index
err, res = fnd3(act, strconv.Itoa(st.Kparentp) + "_Component_" + value, 
                value, "ref_link:...", check, lineNo, lno)
st.K{name}p = res

// type_of: Match child by type name
for id, child := range st.Childs {
    if child.TypeName() == value {
        st.K{name}p = id
        break
    }
}
```

**Pass 2+ - Derived References:**
```go
// ref_copy: Copy pointer from previous field
t := st.K{previous.name}p
if t >= 0 {
    st.K{name}p = act.Ap{previous.comp}[t].K{name}p
}

// ref_child: Look up in previous field's children
if st.K{previous.name}p >= 0 {
    parent := act.Ap{previous.comp}[st.K{previous.name}p].MyName
    err, res = fnd3(act, strconv.Itoa(st.K{previous.name}p) + "_" + value, ...)
    st.K{name}p = res
}

// up_copy: Walk parent chain to find ancestor type
p = st.Me
// Walk up parent chain checking each level
p = act.ApComp[p].Kparentp
// ... until match found
st.K{name}p = p
```

**Why Multiple Passes:**
- ref_child needs previous field resolved first
- ref_copy needs source reference resolved
- up_copy needs parent chain established
- Convergence typically in 2-4 iterations

**Error Handling Strategy:**
Track errors per pass. Stop when:
- All references resolve (errs == 0), OR
- Error count stabilizes (no progress between passes)

**Critical Pattern:**
Always check `K{name}p >= 0` before dereferencing.
Initialize all pointers to -1 to detect unresolved refs.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_field_encoding_patterns
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = data_representation
  overview = "Fields are encoded in generated structs differently based on their type, with value fields in Names map and reference fields as typed pointers."
  doc = ~~~
**Value Fields (in Names map):**
```go
type KpComponent struct {
    Names map[string]any
    // key, word, text, number, tree all go in Names
}

// Loading:
p, st.Names["fieldname"] = getw(ln, p)      // word
p, st.Names["fieldname"] = getws(ln, p)     // text

// Access:
value, ok := st.Names["fieldname"].(string)
```

**Reference Fields (as typed pointers):**
```go
type KpComponent struct {
    Kfieldnamep int    // Pointer to referenced component
    // -1 means unresolved/null
}

// Loading (input from file):
p, st.Kfieldname = getw(ln, p)  // Read key value

// Resolution (later pass):
err, res = fnd3(act, lookup_key, ...)
st.Kfieldnamep = res            // Store resolved index

// Usage:
if st.Kfieldnamep >= 0 {
    target := glob.Dats.ApTargetComp[st.Kfieldnamep]
}
```

**Special Metadata Fields:**
```go
st.Me = len(act.ApComponent)           // My array index
st.MyName = key_value                  // My lookup key
st.Parent = parent_key                 // Parent's key
st.Kparentp = len(act.ApParent) - 1   // Parent's index
st.LineNo = lno                        // Source location
st.Comp = "Component"                  // Type name
st.Names["kComp"] = st.Comp            // Type in payload
st.Names["kMe"] = strconv.Itoa(st.Me)  // Index in payload
st.Names["kParentp"] = strconv.Itoa(st.Kparentp)
```

**Naming Convention:**
- `K{name}` - string value from input file (key/word/text)
- `K{name}p` - integer pointer to resolved component (-1 if unresolved)
- Lowercase in Names map, PascalCase in struct fields
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_index_building
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = lookup_optimization
  overview = "Find and FindIn components build lookup indices during loading to enable fast reference resolution."
  doc = ~~~
**Find (Global Index):**
```go
// For top-level components with Find mode
act.index["Component_" + key_value] = st.Me

// Lookup:
en, exists := glob.Dats.index["Component_" + lookup_key]
if exists {
    component := glob.Dats.ApComponent[en]
}
```

**FindIn (Scoped Index):**
```go
// For nested components with FindIn mode
// Key includes parent pointer for scope
s := strconv.Itoa(st.Kparentp) + "_Component_" + key_value
act.index[s] = st.Me

// Lookup:
lookup_key := strconv.Itoa(parent_id) + "_Component_" + name
en, exists := glob.Dats.index[lookup_key]
```

**Index Building Rules:**
- Only components with Find or FindIn need indices
- Index key must be unique within scope
- Built during load() function, before refs()
- Element with type=key determines the index key
- First key field wins if multiple exist

**Actor Pattern for Index Building:**
```
Actor index Comp find = Find
    Its Element index_name

Actor index_name Element type = key
    C act.index["${comp_name}_" + name] = st.Me
    C st.MyName = name
    Break loop
```

**Why Indices Matter:**
Without indices, every ref lookup requires O(n) linear scan.
With indices, lookup is O(1) hash table access.
Critical for performance on large schemas.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_parent_child_linking
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = hierarchy_management
  overview = "Parent-child relationships are bidirectional: children know parent pointer, parents maintain typed child arrays."
  doc = ~~~
**Child → Parent (Kparentp field):**
```go
// During child load, link to most recent parent
st.Kparentp = len(act.ApParentComp) - 1

if st.Kparentp < 0 {
    // Error: no parent exists
    return 1
}

// Store parent's key for validation
st.Parent = act.ApParentComp[st.Kparentp].MyName
```

**Parent → Children (typed arrays):**
```go
// Parent struct has typed array per child type
type KpParent struct {
    ItsChildType [] *KpChildType
    Childs [] Kp  // Generic child array
}

// During child load, append to parent's arrays
parent := act.ApParentComp[len(act.ApParentComp) - 1]
parent.Childs = append(parent.Childs, st)
parent.ItsChildType = append(parent.ItsChildType, st)
```

**Why Bidirectional:**
- Child needs parent for up_copy and parent traversal
- Parent needs children for Its{Type} iteration
- Typed arrays enable type-safe traversal
- Generic Childs array supports type_of references

**Actor Pattern:**
```
Actor parent_field Comp
    C Kparentp int

Actor parent_field_p Comp parent = SomeComp
    C st.Kparentp = len(act.ApSomeComp) - 1
    C if st.Kparentp < 0 { return 1 }
    C st.Parent = act.ApSomeComp[st.Kparentp].MyName
    C parent := act.ApSomeComp[len(act.ApSomeComp)-1]
    C parent.Childs = append(parent.Childs, st)
    C parent.Its${child_type} = append(parent.Its${child_type}, st)
```

**Validation Point:**
Compare loaded "parent" field value with actual st.Parent.
Catches mismatched parent specifications in input.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_doits_getvar_dispatch
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = operation_dispatch
  overview = "DoIts() and GetVar() implement path-based navigation, dispatching to appropriate handlers based on first path segment."
  doc = ~~~
**DoIts Pattern (Execute Operation):**
```go
func (me KpComponent) DoIts(glob *GlobT, va []string, lno string) int {
    // Reference field navigation
    if va[0] == "fieldname" {
        if me.Kfieldnamep >= 0 {
            st := glob.Dats.ApTargetComp[me.Kfieldnamep]
            if len(va) > 1 {
                return st.DoIts(glob, va[1:], lno)  // Recurse
            }
            return GoAct(glob, st)  // Execute actor
        }
        return 0
    }
    
    // Parent navigation
    if va[0] == "parent" {
        if me.Kparentp >= 0 {
            st := glob.Dats.ApParentComp[me.Kparentp]
            if len(va) > 1 {
                return st.DoIts(glob, va[1:], lno)
            }
            return GoAct(glob, st)
        }
        return 0
    }
    
    // Child type iteration
    if va[0] == "ChildType" {
        for _, st := range me.ItsChildType {
            if len(va) > 1 {
                ret := st.DoIts(glob, va[1:], lno)
                if ret != 0 { return ret }
                continue
            }
            ret := GoAct(glob, st)
            if ret != 0 { return ret }
        }
        return 0
    }
    
    // No match
    fmt.Printf("?No its %s for Component?", va[0])
    return 0
}
```

**GetVar Pattern (Introspection):**
```go
func (me KpComponent) GetVar(glob *GlobT, va []string, lno string) (bool, string) {
    // Reference field navigation
    if va[0] == "fieldname" {
        if me.Kfieldnamep >= 0 && len(va) > 1 {
            return glob.Dats.ApTargetComp[me.Kfieldnamep].GetVar(glob, va[1:], lno)
        }
    }
    
    // Parent navigation
    if va[0] == "parent" {
        if me.Kparentp >= 0 && len(va) > 1 {
            return glob.Dats.ApParentComp[me.Kparentp].GetVar(glob, va[1:], lno)
        }
    }
    
    // Previous sibling
    if va[0] == "previous" {
        if me.Me > 0 && len(va) > 1 {
            return glob.Dats.ApComponent[me.Me - 1].GetVar(glob, va[1:], lno)
        }
    }
    
    // Direct field access (leaf)
    if len(va) == 1 {
        r := me.Names[va[0]]
        if r == nil {
            return false, "?" + va[0] + "?"
        }
        return true, me.Names[va[0]].(string)
    }
    
    return false, "?Unknown path?"
}
```

**Path Syntax Examples:**
- `Component.fieldname` - navigate reference
- `Component.parent` - walk up hierarchy
- `Component.ChildType` - iterate children
- `Component.fieldname.subfieldname` - nested navigation
- `Component.previous.name` - sibling access

**Critical Pattern:**
Always check `len(va)` to distinguish:
- `len(va) > 1` - intermediate navigation, recurse
- `len(va) == 1` - leaf access, return value/execute
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_loader_function_generation
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = parsing
  overview = "Loader functions parse input lines into component instances, building structures and indices during single-pass parsing."
  doc = ~~~
**Loader Function Pattern:**
```go
func loadComponent(act *ActT, ln string, pos int, lno string, 
                   flag []string, names map[string]any) int {
    p := pos
    st := new(KpComponent)
    st.Names = names  // Inherit from parent context
    st.Me = len(act.ApComponent)
    st.LineNo = lno
    st.Comp = "Component"
    st.Flags = flag
    
    // Standard metadata
    st.Names["kComp"] = st.Comp
    st.Names["kMe"] = strconv.Itoa(st.Me)
    st.Names["_lno"] = lno
    
    // Parse each field from input line
    p, st.Names["name"] = getw(ln, p)       // key field
    p, st.Names["type"] = getw(ln, p)       // word field
    p, st.Names["doc"] = getws(ln, p)       // text field
    
    // Initialize reference pointers
    st.Kfieldnamep = -1
    st.Kotherrefp = -1
    
    // Link to parent
    st.Kparentp = len(act.ApParentComp) - 1
    if st.Kparentp >= 0 {
        st.Parent = act.ApParentComp[st.Kparentp].MyName
        parent := act.ApParentComp[st.Kparentp]
        parent.Childs = append(parent.Childs, st)
        parent.ItsComponent = append(parent.ItsComponent, st)
    }
    
    // Build index if Find/FindIn
    if st.Names["name"] != nil {
        name := st.Names["name"].(string)
        act.index["Component_" + name] = st.Me
        st.MyName = name
    }
    
    // Add to global array
    act.ApComponent = append(act.ApComponent, st)
    return 0
}
```

**Loader Variations:**

**Actor Components (no Names map):**
```go
func loadActor(act *ActT, ln string, pos int, lno string, flag []string) int {
    st := new(KpActor)
    // Direct struct fields instead of Names map
    p, st.Kname = getw(ln, p)
    p, st.Kcomp = getw(ln, p)
    // ...
}
```

**Data Components (with Names map):**
```go
func loadComp(act *ActT, ln string, pos int, lno string, 
              flag []string, names map[string]any) int {
    st := new(KpComp)
    st.Names = names  // Key difference
    // All fields go into Names map
}
```

**Helper Functions:**
- `getw(ln, p)` - parse next word (to whitespace)
- `getws(ln, p)` - parse rest of line (text field)
- Return new position `p` for sequential parsing

**Critical Insight:**
Loaders build structure, indices, and parent-child links in ONE PASS.
Reference resolution happens LATER in refs() function.
This separation enables multi-pass reference resolution.
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_error_handling_validation
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = error_management
  overview = "Error tracking accumulates issues during reference resolution and validation, with detailed source location reporting."
  doc = ~~~
**Error Accumulation Pattern:**
```go
func refs(act *ActT) int {
    errs := 0  // Accumulator
    
    for _, st := range act.ApComponent {
        // Attempt resolution
        err, res := fnd3(act, lookup_key, value, context, check, lineNo, lno)
        st.Kfieldnamep = res
        if !err {
            errs += 1  // Count failures
        }
    }
    
    return errs  // Total error count
}
```

**Check Field Validation:**
```
Element comp ref TargetComp .    // check="." - error if not resolved and not "."
Element comp ref TargetComp +    // check="+" - error if not resolved
Element comp ref TargetComp 1    // check="1" - error if not found OR multiple found
Element comp ref TargetComp *    // check="*" - optional, no error
```

**Error Message Pattern:**
```go
if !err && check != "*" {
    fmt.Printf("ref_child:%s.%s unresolved from %s:%s.%s:%s %s > %s\n",
               comp_name, field_name,
               prev_field_type, comp_name, prev_field_name, prev_comp_name,
               lineNo, generator_lno)
    errs += 1
}
```

**Components of Error Message:**
- `ref_child:` - What kind of reference
- `Comp.field` - Which component and field failed
- `from type:Comp.prevfield:PrevComp` - Source reference context
- `lineNo` - Source file line number
- `generator_lno` - Generator actor line number

**Validation Strategy:**

**During refs() passes:**
- Track error count each pass
- Continue if errors decrease (progress being made)
- Stop if errors stabilize (no more progress possible)
- Typically converges in 2-4 passes

**Check field determines strictness:**
- `.` - Error unless explicitly null reference
- `+` - Error if unresolved
- `1` - Error if ambiguous or missing
- `*` - Always succeed (optional reference)

**Critical Pattern:**
Always initialize reference pointers to -1.
This distinguishes "not yet resolved" from "resolved to index 0".

**Error Recovery:**
Unresolved references left at -1 are detected at runtime:
```go
if st.Kfieldnamep >= 0 {
    // Safe to dereference
} else {
    // Gracefully skip or report
}
```
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_ko_interface_implementation
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = interface_pattern
  overview = "All generated components implement the Ko interface (DoIts, GetVar, GetLineNo, TypeName) enabling uniform polymorphic operations."
  doc = ~~~
**The Ko Interface:**
```go
type Kp interface {
    DoIts(glob *GlobT, va []string, lno string) int
    GetVar(glob *GlobT, va []string, lno string) (bool, string)
    GetLineNo() string
    TypeName() string
}
```

**Why This Interface:**
- Enables polymorphic collections (Childs [] Kp)
- Uniform operation dispatch across all types
- Supports type_of references (runtime type checking)
- Foundation for aspect-oriented tracing/validation
- Enables meta-circular operations

**TypeName Implementation:**
```go
func (me KpComponent) TypeName() string {
    return me.Comp  // "Component"
}
```
Used by type_of references to match child by type.

**GetLineNo Implementation:**
```go
func (me KpComponent) GetLineNo() string {
    return me.LineNo  // Source location
}
```
Enables error reporting with source context.

**Polymorphic Child Arrays:**
```go
type KpParent struct {
    Childs [] Kp  // Can hold any component type
}

// Usage:
for _, child := range parent.Childs {
    if child.TypeName() == "SpecificType" {
        child.DoIts(glob, path, lno)  // Polymorphic dispatch
    }
}
```

**Actor Components vs Data Components:**

**Actor Components (compile-time known structure):**
- Don't need Ko interface (static dispatch)
- No Names map (direct struct fields)
- No runtime type checking needed

**Data Components (runtime-variable structure):**
- MUST implement Ko interface
- Names map for flexible fields
- Support runtime navigation and type checking

**When to Generate Ko Interface:**
```
Actor struct Comp name = Actor
    // NO Ko interface, static dispatch

Actor struct Comp parent = Actor  
    // NO Ko interface, static dispatch

Actor struct Comp
    // YES Ko interface, dynamic dispatch
```

**Critical Insight:**
Ko interface is not just convenience - it's the foundation for:
- Aspect-oriented tracing (universal hooks)
- Meta-circular execution (code operating on code)
- Runtime schema evolution (dynamic types)
- Autonomous learning (observing all operations)
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_codegen_decision_tree
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = decision_guide
  overview = "Decision tree for generating correct code based on component and element attributes."
  doc = ~~~
**Component Type Determines Structure:**

Q: Is this an Actor component?
├─ YES: Generate without Ko interface, no Names map, direct fields
│   - Pattern: `Actor struct Comp name = Actor`
│   - Pattern: `Actor struct Comp parent = Actor`
│   - Load function: loadActor(act, ln, pos, lno, flag)
│   - Fields: Direct struct fields (Kname, Kcomp, etc.)
│
└─ NO: Generate with Ko interface, Names map, polymorphic
    - Pattern: `Actor struct Comp`
    - Load function: loadComp(act, ln, pos, lno, flag, names)
    - Fields: Names map[string]any

**Find Mode Determines Indexing:**

Q: What is component's find mode?
├─ Find: Global top-level index
│   - Key: "ComponentName_" + key_value
│   - Pattern: `Actor index Comp find = Find`
│
├─ FindIn: Scoped parent-relative index
│   - Key: parent_id + "_ComponentName_" + key_value
│   - Pattern: `Actor index Comp find = FindIn`
│
└─ ".": No indexing
    - No index generation needed

**Element Type Determines Field Generation:**

Q: What is element type?
├─ key, word, text, number, tree
│   - Value field in Names map or struct
│   - Loading: getw() or getws()
│   - No pointer field needed
│
├─ ref, link
│   - Parse: K{name} string (input value)
│   - Pointer: K{name}p int (resolved index)
│   - Resolution: Pass 1 (direct lookup)
│
├─ type_of
│   - Pointer: K{name}p int (child array index)
│   - Resolution: Pass 1 (child type matching)
│
├─ up_copy
│   - Pointer: K{name}p int (ancestor index)
│   - Resolution: Pass 1 (parent chain walk)
│
├─ ref_copy
│   - Pointer: K{name}p int (copied from previous)
│   - Resolution: Pass 2 (depends on previous field)
│
└─ ref_child
    - Parse: K{name} string (lookup key)
    - Pointer: K{name}p int (child index)
    - Resolution: Pass 2 (depends on previous field)

**Check Field Determines Validation:**

Q: What is check value?
├─ "." → Error if unresolved AND target not "."
├─ "+" → Error if unresolved
├─ "1" → Error if unresolved OR ambiguous
└─ "*" → No validation, optional

**Parent Relationship Determines Linking:**

Q: Does component have parent?
├─ YES → Generate Kparentp field
│   - Link during load
│   - Append to parent's ItsChildType array
│   - Append to parent's generic Childs array
│
└─ NO → Top-level component
    - No parent pointer needed
    - Add to global index if Find mode

**Code Generation Decision:**
IF Actor component → Static, no Ko, no Names
IF Data component → Dynamic, Ko interface, Names map
IF Find mode → Global index
IF FindIn mode → Scoped index
IF ref/link/type_of/up_copy → Pass 1 resolution
IF ref_copy/ref_child → Pass 2+ resolution
~~~
}

Canon {
  name = actor_codegen_best_practices
  category = code_generation
  topic_type = guidelines
  overview = "Proven practices for generating correct, maintainable, and performant code from actor schemas."
  doc = ~~~
**1. Always Initialize Reference Pointers:**
```go
st.Kfieldnamep = -1  // Not 0!
```
Zero is a valid array index. -1 clearly means "unresolved".

**2. Separate Value Parsing from Resolution:**
```go
// During load: Parse string value
p, st.Kfieldname = getw(ln, p)

// During refs: Resolve to pointer
err, res := fnd3(act, lookup_key, ...)
st.Kfieldnamep = res
```
Never try to resolve during load - indices not built yet.

**3. Check Array Bounds Before Access:**
```go
if st.Kfieldnamep >= 0 && st.Kfieldnamep < len(act.ApTargetComp) {
    target := act.ApTargetComp[st.Kfieldnamep]
}
```
Handle unresolved references gracefully.

**4. Preserve Source Location Context:**
```go
st.LineNo = lno                    // Where in source file
st.Names["_lno"] = lno             // Also in payload
// Use in error messages
fmt.Printf("Error at %s\n", st.LineNo)
```
Critical for debugging generated code.

**5. Build Indices Before Resolution:**
```
1. Load all components (build structures)
2. Build all indices (Find/FindIn)
3. Resolve references (multi-pass)
```
Order matters - can't resolve without indices.

**6. Handle Optional vs Required Fields:**
```go
// Required (check = "+" or "1"):
if st.Kfieldnamep < 0 {
    errs += 1  // Error
}

// Optional (check = "*"):
if st.Kfieldnamep >= 0 {
    // Use if available
}
```
Check field controls strictness.

**7. Use Typed Child Arrays:**
```go
// Don't iterate generic Childs and filter by type:
for _, child := range parent.Childs {
    if child.TypeName() == "Element" { ... }  // Slow
}

// Do use typed array:
for _, elem := range parent.ItsElement { ... }  // Fast
```
Type-specific arrays are O(n) instead of O(n*m).

**8. Accumulate Errors, Don't Fail Fast:**
```go
errs := 0
for _, st := range components {
    if !validate(st) {
        errs += 1  // Count, don't return
    }
}
return errs  // Report all errors at once
```
User sees all problems, not just first one.

**9. Generate Consistent Naming:**
- Component types: PascalCase (KpComponent)
- Field names: lowercase (Kfieldname)
- Reference pointers: lowercase + p (Kfieldnamep)
- Arrays: Ap + PascalCase (ApComponent)
- Child arrays: Its + PascalCase (ItsElement)

**10. Comment with Generator Line Numbers:**
```go
C // ${._lno}
```
Links generated code back to generator actor.
Invaluable for debugging generator issues.

**11. Handle Name Collisions:**
Names map can hold same key from different contexts:
```go
st.Names["kComp"] = "Component"    // Type name
st.Names["kMe"] = "123"            // Array index
st.Names["fieldname"] = "value"    // Actual field
```
Use prefixes (k, _, K) to avoid collisions.

**12. Test Multi-Pass Convergence:**
```go
prev_errs := 999999
for pass := 0; pass < 10; pass++ {
    errs := refs(act)
    if errs == 0 {
        break  // Success
    }
    if errs == prev_errs {
        break  // Stuck, no progress
    }
    prev_errs = errs
}
```
Detect both success and deadlock conditions.
~~~
}

